# API standards

## Base path and resources

- Base path: `/api`.
- Resources: plural nouns (`/api/tickets`, `/api/tickets/{id}`).
- Status changes: `POST /api/tickets/{id}/status` with body `{ "status": "IN_PROGRESS" }` — not mixed into generic PATCH without validation.
- Comments: `POST /api/tickets/{id}/comments`.

## List, search, filter

- `GET /api/tickets` supports:
  - `status` — exact match on ticket status enum.
  - `q` — keyword search on title and description (backend-defined, documented in spec).
  - `page`, `size` — optional pagination (0-based or 1-based per spec; stay consistent).

## HTTP semantics

| Situation | Status |
|-----------|--------|
| Validation failure | 400 |
| Missing ticket | 404 |
| Invalid status transition | 409 |
| Success create | 201 |
| Success read/update | 200 |

## Error JSON (consistent shape)

Use a single problem style across endpoints, for example:

```json
{
  "status": 400,
  "title": "Validation failed",
  "detail": "One or more fields are invalid",
  "errors": [
    { "field": "title", "message": "must not be blank" }
  ]
}
```

For 409 transitions, include `detail` with human-readable reason (e.g. `Cannot transition from CLOSED to OPEN`).

## Documentation

- Keep `spec/api-contract.md` in sync with controllers.
- Expose OpenAPI via springdoc (`/swagger-ui.html` or `/swagger-ui/index.html`).

## CORS

- Local dev: allow `http://localhost:3000` only.
- Do not commit wildcard CORS for production profiles.
